{"availability":"available","full":"ahmed-elliethy/two_level_qr","name":"two_level_qr","description":"A Dart SDK that implements a keyed two-level QR mode that hides a secret message during encoding of a QR. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"Dart","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-24T13:10:45Z","updated":"2026-10-03T07:35:36Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://twolevelqrdemo.pages.dev","topics":[],"demo":"https://twolevelqrdemo.pages.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.121Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.121Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.121Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.121Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Dart SDK that implements a keyed two-level QR mode that hides a secret message during encoding of a QR. The hiding is performed within the Reed-Solomon error-correction channel by introducing deliberate errors. Reed-Solomon correction restores the original public data, while the difference between the raw and corrected codewords carries the hidden payload. A position key controls which positions carry the secret, and an optional encryption passphrase encrypts the payload with authenticated encryption (AES-SIV or ChaCha20-Poly1305) so it stays confidential. The SDK also supports a full QR…","A normal QR code carries one message. A two-level QR code carries two:","The encoder deliberately introduces byte errors into the Reed-Solomon codewords. The values of those errors are the hidden bytes. A normal scanner performs Reed-Solomon error correction, removes errors, and reads the public text. The TwoLevelQR decoder does the same, but also compares the raw codewords against the corrected codewords at key-derived positions to recover the hidden bytes."],"features":["Full encode/decode pipeline (segments → data codewords → RS ECC → interleave → matrix)","First-class checkpoints at every stage (EncodeResult, DecodeResult)","Keyed hidden message channel using deliberate byte errors","Encrypted hidden messages with pluggable ciphers: AES-SIV (default) and ChaCha20-Poly1305 built in, or bring your own by implementing HiddenMessageCipher","Configurable error-budget ratio for the hidden channel; encryption overhead always stays within it"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ahmed-elliethy/two_level_qr/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"af822a309e1ae02e92c7cb1d48fe312e4c7c25b445dff98aa939acfb947060c5","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.298Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.298Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Dart SDK that implements a keyed two-level QR mode that hides a secret message during encoding of a QR. The hiding is performed within the Reed-Solomon error-correction channel by introducing deliberate errors. Reed-Solomon correction restores the original public data, while the difference between the raw and corrected codewords carries the hidden payload. A position key controls which positions carry the secret, and an optional encryption passphrase encrypts the payload with authenticated encryption (AES-SIV or ChaCha20-Poly1305) so it stays confidential. The SDK also supports a full QR…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ahmed-elliethy/two_level_qr/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"af822a309e1ae02e92c7cb1d48fe312e4c7c25b445dff98aa939acfb947060c5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ahmed-elliethy/two_level_qr/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.298Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T07:35:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ahmed-elliethy/two_level_qr/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:21.299Z","hash":"af822a309e1ae02e92c7cb1d48fe312e4c7c25b445dff98aa939acfb947060c5","originalBytes":19974,"storedBytes":19974,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["hidden","message","cipher","level","bytes","key","payload","ratio","ciphers","dart","public","byte","